- d2 `.mise.toml` all: **rewrite**. New fork-only file pinning mise's rust to the channel rust-toolchain.toml already requests (nightly-2026-11-08), so a mise user resolves the same toolchain; rust-toolchain.toml keeps the components/targets mise cannot express. It does not by itself unblock the build: the build service reads mise config before rust-toolchain.toml, so the rust pin's source is always 'rust-toolchain.toml' and is dropped whenever rustup is on the job PATH (verified by running the planner's own pins()/wrap() against this tree). Kept minimal and documented; created as the orchestrator directed.
- d3 `.cargo/rustc` all: **rewrite**. Cargo invokes the wrapper with cwd set to the crate being built, so rustup's sibling shim resolved the toolchain from that crate directory and missed the workspace pin, falling back to the active/default stable toolchain (1.85 in the build service) which rejects the workspace's `-Z embed-metadata` ("the option `Z` is only accepted on the nightly compiler"). Naming the channel explicitly with `rustup run <channel> rustc/rustdoc "$@"` forces the pinned toolchain regardless of cwd or RUSTUP_TOOLCHAIN. The channel is derived from the root rust-toolchain.toml (found relative to the wrapper's own absolute path) with an explicit nightly-2026-11-08 fallback, and the PATH tool is still used when rustup is unavailable, preserving the original fallback.
- d4 `.cargo/rustdoc` all: **rewrite**. Cargo invokes the wrapper with cwd set to the crate being built, so rustup's sibling shim resolved the toolchain from that crate directory and missed the workspace pin, falling back to the active/default stable toolchain (1.85 in the build service) which rejects the workspace's `-Z embed-metadata` ("the option `Z` is only accepted on the nightly compiler"). Naming the channel explicitly with `rustup run <channel> rustc/rustdoc "$@"` forces the pinned toolchain regardless of cwd or RUSTUP_TOOLCHAIN. The channel is derived from the root rust-toolchain.toml (found relative to the wrapper's own absolute path) with an explicit nightly-2026-11-08 fallback, and the PATH tool is still used when rustup is unavailable, preserving the original fallback.
- d5 `.cargo/config.toml` [build]: **rewrite**. Adds the [build] rustc/rustdoc keys that route the compiler through the wrappers, so the pinned nightly is used even when a distribution/Nix rustc comes first on PATH. Without these keys the wrappers are never invoked and the build keeps failing on `-Z`.

